    "OT_VERSE_REF": "Micah 6:8",
    "OT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "What does the LORD require of you but to do justice, and to love kindness, and to walk humbly with your God?",
    "NT_VERSE_REF": "2 Corinthians 5:7",
    "NT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "For we walk by faith, not by sight.",
    "OT_VERSE_LINE": "Micah 6:8 — “What does the LORD require of you but to do justice, and to love kindness, and to walk humbly with your God?”",
    "NT_VERSE_LINE": "2 Corinthians 5:7 — “For we walk by faith, not by sight.”",
    "GREEK": "περιπατέω",
    "GREEK_TRANSLIT": "peripateo",
    "HEBREW": "הָלַךְ",
    "HEBREW_TRANSLIT": "halakh",
    "OT_REFS": "Gen 5:24 • Gen 6:9 • Ps 23:4 • Isa 40:31",
    "NT_REFS": "Eph 4:1 • Eph 5:2 • 1 John 1:7 • 3 John 1:4",
    "TRIVIA_BULLETS": [
      "The Hebrew root *halakh* forms *Halakhah*, the body of Jewish law, literally meaning \"the way to walk.\"",
      "Enoch and Noah are the only two individuals in the Bible explicitly described as having \"walked with God.\"",
      "The Greek *peripateo* (literally \"walk around\") is used dozens of times to describe one's daily conduct or lifestyle."
